[[:db/retract 17592186129666 :question/answer-fields 17592186127477] {:db/id 17592186129134 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d6880ebc-9daa-5cd0-b5d7-2100fa039d06"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129666 :question/problem "$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -6 \\\\ 6 & -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the vector $v$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $v$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-7-6\\text{i},$ find a matrix $P$ such that $A=PC{P}^{-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\nFirst, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -6 \\\\ 6 & -7\\end{aligned}]=C.\n$$\n\nNext, we can find the real and imaginary parts of our eigenvector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]={{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(v)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(v)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now construct $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ca3e15c9-c3c6-56d5-be44-2ff142682b75"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ca3e15c9-c3c6-56d5-be44-2ff142682b75" :answer-field/id #uuid "ca3e15c9-c3c6-56d5-be44-2ff142682b75" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dd8d4b33-9126-5017-a544-498f72884d7e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d4ea0660-35e1-50a9-b795-bedb0a6fec90" "answer-1b240860-8981-5813-8afb-56eb81d9d5f3" "answer-03ce9065-737f-5539-9ccc-e2b738124790" "answer-dd8d4b33-9126-5017-a544-498f72884d7e" "answer-ed49cec1-2e8a-5d58-9643-ab871cbaf80d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4ea0660-35e1-50a9-b795-bedb0a6fec90" :answer/id #uuid "d4ea0660-35e1-50a9-b795-bedb0a6fec90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b240860-8981-5813-8afb-56eb81d9d5f3" :answer/id #uuid "1b240860-8981-5813-8afb-56eb81d9d5f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03ce9065-737f-5539-9ccc-e2b738124790" :answer/id #uuid "03ce9065-737f-5539-9ccc-e2b738124790" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd8d4b33-9126-5017-a544-498f72884d7e" :answer/id #uuid "dd8d4b33-9126-5017-a544-498f72884d7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ed49cec1-2e8a-5d58-9643-ab871cbaf80d" :answer/id #uuid "ed49cec1-2e8a-5d58-9643-ab871cbaf80d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129136 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-59a82201-03c5-57db-ad1f-7c04fbb98da0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-59a82201-03c5-57db-ad1f-7c04fbb98da0" :question/id #uuid "59a82201-03c5-57db-ad1f-7c04fbb98da0" :question/math-academy-id "q-39157" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}16 & -10 \\\\ 17 & -10\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above.\nGiven that $A$ has the complex eigenvalue $\\lambda =3-\\text{i},$ and that $A=PC{P}^{-1}$ where $C$ is a rotation-scaling matrix, what is the value of \n$\\frac{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}{{c}^{2}+{d}^{2}}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\nSince we are given the eigenvalue $\\lambda =3-\\text{i},$ we can immediately construct the rotation-scaling matrix:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\text{x}=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\,{\\lambda }_{1}=3-\\text{i},$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}16 & -10 \\\\ 17 & -10\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3-\\text{i} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}13+\\text{i} & -10 \\\\ 17 & -13+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the homogeneous system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}(13+\\text{i}){x}_{1}-10{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 17{x}_{1}+(-13+\\text{i}){x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix $A-\\lambda I$ is singular, the system above must have a non-zero solution. This means that one equation of the system is a multiple of another. As a result, we can drop one of the rows and take one of the variables as the free variable. For example, from the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{10}(13+\\text{i}){x}_{1}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ \\frac{1}{10}(13+\\text{i}){x}_{1}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{1}\\in C.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{1}=10$, we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 13+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can construct the matrix $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}10 & 0 \\\\ 13 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}{{c}^{2}+{d}^{2}}=\\frac{{10}^{2}+{0}^{2}}{{13}^{2}+{1}^{2}}=\\frac{10}{17}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7cbd9e54-5f08-5851-844d-53c1919540be"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7cbd9e54-5f08-5851-844d-53c1919540be" :answer-field/id #uuid "7cbd9e54-5f08-5851-844d-53c1919540be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3060d69a-8868-5172-98ad-30a1f7c52b08" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3060d69a-8868-5172-98ad-30a1f7c52b08" "answer-d1e1a656-0f4d-5746-87e0-6a88b18aafd0" "answer-95fee729-2135-5651-b276-0d9f45ed5e6c" "answer-5205fd9c-21af-5e9d-977c-cdc6794be310" "answer-4fac5dc4-ba16-5d80-bb5f-c21a117180c3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3060d69a-8868-5172-98ad-30a1f7c52b08" :answer/id #uuid "3060d69a-8868-5172-98ad-30a1f7c52b08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10}{17}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d1e1a656-0f4d-5746-87e0-6a88b18aafd0" :answer/id #uuid "d1e1a656-0f4d-5746-87e0-6a88b18aafd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{18}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95fee729-2135-5651-b276-0d9f45ed5e6c" :answer/id #uuid "95fee729-2135-5651-b276-0d9f45ed5e6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14}{17}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5205fd9c-21af-5e9d-977c-cdc6794be310" :answer/id #uuid "5205fd9c-21af-5e9d-977c-cdc6794be310" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15}{19}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4fac5dc4-ba16-5d80-bb5f-c21a117180c3" :answer/id #uuid "4fac5dc4-ba16-5d80-bb5f-c21a117180c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{19}{14}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d6880ebc-9daa-5cd0-b5d7-2100fa039d06" :question/id #uuid "d6880ebc-9daa-5cd0-b5d7-2100fa039d06" :question/math-academy-id "q-99345" :question/problem "$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}-1+\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the vector $v$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $v$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =4+3\\text{i},$ find a matrix $P$ such that $A=PC{P}^{-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\nFirst, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]=C.\n$$\n\nNext, we can find the real and imaginary parts of our eigenvector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =[\\begin{aligned}-1+\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(v)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(v)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now construct $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8400b796-2f04-536c-986d-13f15ae5b122"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8400b796-2f04-536c-986d-13f15ae5b122" :answer-field/id #uuid "8400b796-2f04-536c-986d-13f15ae5b122" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f16edcb8-7daa-5bb4-b079-ab44c7accef8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5113c383-2506-5331-9225-ebb1f5af24a3" "answer-0a8fe61d-12cc-5e71-bf5f-8ade179fac6d" "answer-096e7527-4c01-5dce-8ff8-e0db3c75370d" "answer-f16edcb8-7daa-5bb4-b079-ab44c7accef8" "answer-1c87451a-2d1c-5373-8af0-e4594174b876"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5113c383-2506-5331-9225-ebb1f5af24a3" :answer/id #uuid "5113c383-2506-5331-9225-ebb1f5af24a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a8fe61d-12cc-5e71-bf5f-8ade179fac6d" :answer/id #uuid "0a8fe61d-12cc-5e71-bf5f-8ade179fac6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-096e7527-4c01-5dce-8ff8-e0db3c75370d" :answer/id #uuid "096e7527-4c01-5dce-8ff8-e0db3c75370d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f16edcb8-7daa-5bb4-b079-ab44c7accef8" :answer/id #uuid "f16edcb8-7daa-5bb4-b079-ab44c7accef8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c87451a-2d1c-5373-8af0-e4594174b876" :answer/id #uuid "1c87451a-2d1c-5373-8af0-e4594174b876" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129214 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b89eb3d0-aaac-5e32-8106-610f887f220d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b89eb3d0-aaac-5e32-8106-610f887f220d" :question/id #uuid "b89eb3d0-aaac-5e32-8106-610f887f220d" :question/math-academy-id "q-99416" :question/problem "$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}-3\\text{i} \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the vector $v$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $v$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1+3\\text{i},$ find a matrix $P$ such that $A=PC{P}^{-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\nFirst, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\ne C,\n$$\n\nwhile\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda }) & \\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda }) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda }) & \\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda })\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]=C.\n$$\n\nSo, our rotation-scaling matrix $C$ corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\overset{―}{\\lambda }=-1-3\\text{i},$ \n the complex conjugate of $\\lambda .$ Hence, to construct the matrix $P,$ we use the eigenvector $\\overset{―}{v},$ the complex conjugate of $v.$\n\nNext, we find the real and imaginary parts of our eigenvector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{v} & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\text{i} \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]={{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{v})}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{v})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now construct $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{v}) & \\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{v}) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ba30525c-f325-567a-9297-5b7c22b96813"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ba30525c-f325-567a-9297-5b7c22b96813" :answer-field/id #uuid "ba30525c-f325-567a-9297-5b7c22b96813" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b6dd3430-18a3-5d4c-aa84-56246e5e6e49" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b6dd3430-18a3-5d4c-aa84-56246e5e6e49" "answer-d396ac8a-9e62-5ef7-aa22-08d3e2840f8f" "answer-39b2aad9-d90d-5e0c-99c0-086cce1f5858" "answer-b4f2b609-e44a-59ef-8d01-1bf7e729ec81" "answer-0a822e0b-1fa5-5287-afb1-796b6d1e0af8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b6dd3430-18a3-5d4c-aa84-56246e5e6e49" :answer/id #uuid "b6dd3430-18a3-5d4c-aa84-56246e5e6e49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d396ac8a-9e62-5ef7-aa22-08d3e2840f8f" :answer/id #uuid "d396ac8a-9e62-5ef7-aa22-08d3e2840f8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39b2aad9-d90d-5e0c-99c0-086cce1f5858" :answer/id #uuid "39b2aad9-d90d-5e0c-99c0-086cce1f5858" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4f2b609-e44a-59ef-8d01-1bf7e729ec81" :answer/id #uuid "b4f2b609-e44a-59ef-8d01-1bf7e729ec81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a822e0b-1fa5-5287-afb1-796b6d1e0af8" :answer/id #uuid "0a822e0b-1fa5-5287-afb1-796b6d1e0af8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-5f5420bc-3099-5b53-8e6a-d43b1a5bffb0" :activity/id #uuid "5f5420bc-3099-5b53-8e6a-d43b1a5bffb0" :activity/title "Reducing Real 2x2 Matrices to Rotation-Scaling Form" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048584 :activity/course 17592186046673 :activity/steps ["step-aae2eb64-abfd-507c-b3bc-9c0cd712cf93" "step-8a7b4be3-057a-5a01-ae4d-c3c2e06c7bcc" "step-c04d526e-a848-55ef-9d6a-e6653cc7bbac" "step-43b5ac79-b939-5882-be87-3661f9387201"] :activity/first-step "step-aae2eb64-abfd-507c-b3bc-9c0cd712cf93" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-aae2eb64-abfd-507c-b3bc-9c0cd712cf93" :step/id #uuid "aae2eb64-abfd-507c-b3bc-9c0cd712cf93" :step/content 17592186129666 :step/next "step-8a7b4be3-057a-5a01-ae4d-c3c2e06c7bcc" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-8a7b4be3-057a-5a01-ae4d-c3c2e06c7bcc" :step/id #uuid "8a7b4be3-057a-5a01-ae4d-c3c2e06c7bcc" :step/content "question-59a82201-03c5-57db-ad1f-7c04fbb98da0" :step/next "step-c04d526e-a848-55ef-9d6a-e6653cc7bbac" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c04d526e-a848-55ef-9d6a-e6653cc7bbac" :step/id #uuid "c04d526e-a848-55ef-9d6a-e6653cc7bbac" :step/content "question-d6880ebc-9daa-5cd0-b5d7-2100fa039d06" :step/next "step-43b5ac79-b939-5882-be87-3661f9387201" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-43b5ac79-b939-5882-be87-3661f9387201" :step/id #uuid "43b5ac79-b939-5882-be87-3661f9387201" :step/content "question-b89eb3d0-aaac-5e32-8106-610f887f220d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
